sycl: routing bias and an additive norm guard in the fused top-k MoE

HomeBrain patch on ggml-sycl. Applies on top of 0011.
Upstream tracking: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/32757

The SYCL top-k MoE fusion declined any routing bias, so Inkling's router
(SIGMOID, ADD of a selection bias, ARGSORT, GET_ROWS, then a weight norm) ran as
7 kernels in each of its 48 layer passes per token. This ports CUDA's has_bias
path: experts are selected by prob + bias and weighted by the unbiased prob.
Inkling's norm guards the weight sum with scale_bias(sum, 1, eps), set by
expert_weights_norm_eps > 0, where other models use clamp(sum, min). Neither
backend fused that form; here the guard may be either node.

